          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>Acute promyelocytic leukaemia (FAB M3) carries the translocation t(15;17). Which</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Acute promyelocytic leukaemia (FAB M3) carries the translocation t(15;17). Which life-threatening complication is characteristically associated with this subtype?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Tumour lysis syndrome</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Tumour lysis syndrome can complicate any leukaemia with high blast burden but is not the hallmark complication of APL specifically.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Disseminated intravascular coagulation</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Abnormal promyelocytes release tissue factor, triggering DIC — a dangerous combination of simultaneous bleeding and clotting. ATRA combined with arsenic trioxide overcomes the differentiation block and has made APL the most curable form of AML.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Superior vena cava syndrome</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>SVC syndrome is characteristic of T-cell ALL, where a mediastinal mass from thymic infiltration compresses the great veins, not of APL.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hyperviscosity syndrome</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Hyperviscosity syndrome is associated with paraproteinaemias such as Waldenström macroglobulinaemia, not with APL.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "APL carries a specific risk of DIC because abnormal promyelocytes release tissue factor. Recognising this complication early is critical — it is the leading cause of early death in APL before treatment takes effect."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "DIC is the hallmark of APL. The PML-RARα fusion protein blocks maturation at the promyelocyte stage, and the abnormal cells release tissue factor that triggers the coagulation cascade."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
